2.6.2 Kolmogorov-Smirnov test
The Kolmogorov-Smirnov (KS) statistical test [81] is a non-parametric test that used
to compute bounds on empirical CDFs given N samples. The test is based on the
maximum distance between an empirical CDF and a hypothetical CDF, as follows:
