2.5 shows an example of DS and P-box interchangeability. It is important to mention
that Dempster-Shafer structures can be always translated into P-boxes although that
is not a biunivocal transformation. More specifically, a Dempster-Shafer structure can
be associated to a single Probability box, while a Probability box can be associated to
more than one Dempster-Shafer structure depending on the number of the number n
in the α-slicing procedure (e.g. a low n will correspond to a coarse discretization) [49].
Probability boxes and Dempster-Shafer structures offer a straightforward way to deal
with multiple and overlapping intervals, inconsistent sources of information and small
sample sizes.
