where PpCl|CN´kq is the probability of a secondary (post-contingency) trip of the
line plq after the contingency denoted as CN´k occurred. The severity SlpCN´kq is a
overload severity function for the line l due to the occurrence of a single trip (k “ 1)
or multiple failures (k ą 1).
Severity functions can be used to quantify the operational risk due to components
failures [122]. The continuous severity function for overload is specifically defined for
each circuit (lines and transformers). It measures the extent (severity) of failures in
terms of line percentage of rating P Rl “
