generators (Gen1 and Gen2) are installed as displayed in Fig. 8.2 and controlled to minimize power unbalances on the grid. We assume that the 2 controllable generators and
links 3 and 4 are affected by degradation and, thus, are equipped with PHM capabilities
to inform the decision-maker on their degradation states, then D “ t1, 2, 3, 4u. The two
loads and the two renewable generators define the grid power setting, P “ t5, 6, 7, 8u
